@startuml
title User Stories to Use Cases to Issues to Sprints - UML 2.5.1

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ArrowFontColor #334155
skinparam ActorBorderColor #0F172A
skinparam ActorFontColor #0F172A
skinparam UsecaseBorderColor #1D4ED8
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam UsecaseFontColor #0F172A
skinparam ArtifactBorderColor #475569
skinparam ArtifactBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ArtifactFontColor #0F172A
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

rectangle "Actors" {
  actor "Viewer" as Viewer
  actor "Editor" as Editor
  actor "Admin" as Admin
  actor "Municipality\nIT / Dev Team" as IT
}

rectangle "Permissions" {
  usecase "Viewer\nPermission" as P_VIEW
  usecase "Editor\nPermission" as P_EDIT
  usecase "Admin\nPermission" as P_ADMIN
  usecase "Deployment\nResponsibility" as P_DEPLOY
}

rectangle "Use Cases" {
  usecase "Access control\nand permissions" as UC_ACCESS
  usecase "Search and view\nbuilding records" as UC_VIEW
  usecase "Manage building\nrepository" as UC_MANAGE
  usecase "Import / export\nbuilding data" as UC_DATA
  usecase "Produce\nbuilding cards" as UC_CARDS
  usecase "Review\naudit trail" as UC_LOGS
  usecase "Use GIS\nmap context" as UC_GIS
  usecase "Deploy inside\nmunicipality network" as UC_DEPLOY
  usecase "Prove map provider\nflexibility" as UC_PROVIDER
}

rectangle "User Story Issues" {
  artifact "US #20/#21/#22\nAs an admin, I want role-based access,\n2FA login, and permission control\nso only authorized users can use the system." as US_ACCESS
  artifact "US #23/#24/#25\nAs a viewer, I want to view, search,\nfilter, and open building details\nso I can review records quickly." as US_VIEW
  artifact "US #27/#28/#29\nAs an editor, I want to add, update,\nand safely remove buildings\nso the repository stays current." as US_MANAGE
  artifact "US #76\nAs municipality staff, I want to export\nand restore building data\nso local backup is possible." as US_DATA
  artifact "US #26\nAs a viewer, I want to produce\na building card image\nso it can be used in presentations." as US_CARDS
  artifact "US #30/#31/#32/#34\nAs a viewer/editor/admin, I want logs\nand audit history so building changes\nremain accountable." as US_LOGS
  artifact "US #35/#84/#85\nAs a viewer/editor, I want GIS map context\nand area selection so records connect\nto real locations." as US_GIS
  artifact "US #94\nAs municipality staff, I want GhostHouses\ndeployed on the municipality server\nso it can be used internally." as US_DEPLOY
  artifact "US #91\nAs a viewer, I want an OpenStreetMap proof\nso the team can demonstrate\nmap-provider flexibility." as US_PROVIDER
}

rectangle "Sprints / Branches" {
  artifact "release/stage-a/sprint-2-final\nrelease/stage-b/sprint-3-final" as S_ACCESS
  artifact "release/stage-a/sprint-2-final\nrelease/stage-b/sprint-3-final" as S_VIEW
  artifact "release/stage-a/sprint-1-mvp\nrelease/stage-a/sprint-2-final" as S_MANAGE
  artifact "release/stage-a/sprint-1-mvp\nrelease/stage-a/sprint-2-final" as S_DATA
  artifact "release/stage-a/sprint-2-final\nrelease/stage-b/sprint-2-gis\nrelease/stage-b/sprint-3-final" as S_CARDS
  artifact "release/stage-a/sprint-2-final" as S_LOGS
  artifact "release/stage-b/sprint-2-gis" as S_GIS
  artifact "release/stage-b/sprint-1-deployment" as S_DEPLOY
  artifact "feature/map-provider-flexibility/main\nnot merged to production releases" as S_PROVIDER
}

Viewer --> P_VIEW
Editor --> P_VIEW
Editor --> P_EDIT
Admin --> P_VIEW
Admin --> P_EDIT
Admin --> P_ADMIN
IT --> P_DEPLOY

P_ADMIN --> UC_ACCESS
P_VIEW --> UC_VIEW
P_EDIT --> UC_MANAGE
P_EDIT --> UC_DATA
P_VIEW --> UC_CARDS
P_VIEW --> UC_LOGS
P_EDIT --> UC_LOGS
P_VIEW --> UC_GIS
P_EDIT --> UC_GIS
P_DEPLOY --> UC_DEPLOY
P_DEPLOY --> UC_PROVIDER

UC_ACCESS ..> US_ACCESS : traces to
UC_VIEW ..> US_VIEW : traces to
UC_MANAGE ..> US_MANAGE : traces to
UC_DATA ..> US_DATA : traces to
UC_CARDS ..> US_CARDS : traces to
UC_LOGS ..> US_LOGS : traces to
UC_GIS ..> US_GIS : traces to
UC_DEPLOY ..> US_DEPLOY : traces to
UC_PROVIDER ..> US_PROVIDER : traces to

US_ACCESS ..> S_ACCESS : delivered in
US_VIEW ..> S_VIEW : delivered in
US_MANAGE ..> S_MANAGE : delivered in
US_DATA ..> S_DATA : delivered in
US_CARDS ..> S_CARDS : delivered in
US_LOGS ..> S_LOGS : delivered in
US_GIS ..> S_GIS : delivered in
US_DEPLOY ..> S_DEPLOY : tracked in
US_PROVIDER ..> S_PROVIDER : proof branch
@enduml
